      "writtenOn": "2026-10-05T15:33:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we use the standard `clwb(p)` helper from \u003casm/special_insns.h\u003e here instead of open-coding the inline assembly?\n`clwb(p)` uses ALTERNATIVE_2 (falling back safely to clflushopt/clflush if X86_FEATURE_CLWB isn\u0027t present) and casts p to a 64-byte struct { char x[64]; } * memory operand so the compiler knows the full 64-byte cache line is being accessed rather than just the single byte at *p.",
      "revId": "cf20c42c29ca65d1f3635560410234a7efd6760d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
